# Astronomy Python Tools

Welcome to my collection of Python scripts used for astronomy and astrophysics!

This repository contains Python scripts I've written to support my astronomy classes.

These include tools for:
- Spectral Line Calculations (Balmer Series)
- Orbital Mechanics (Kepler's Laws, Velocity)
- Data Visualizations and Graphing

I created these mainly for studying astronomy and astrophysics. I plan to expand this repository with more scripts to help my research projects.

## Tools

### Fundamentals
- Balmer Series Calculator (Visible Hydrogen Spectral Lines)

### Orbital Mechanics
- Kepler's Third Law Graph
- Orbital Velocity Vs. Distance

### Data Analysis (in progress)
- Light curve plotting tools (for variable stars)

## Languages and Libraries Used
- Python
- NumPy
- Matplotlib
 
